    <name><text>WAT 03.1: Change and Verdict Together!</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<div style="border-left:4px solid #2c3e50; padding:0.5em 1em; margin-bottom:1em; background:#eef1f4;"><b>Goal</b><p>A ticket clerk gives each traveller both a ticket and any money owed as change. When the payment covers the fare, the traveller gets the change and a ticket, reported as <code>true</code>. When the payment falls short, the clerk refuses, so the change is <code>0</code> and the ticket verdict is <code>false</code>. A concession traveller pays half the fare, rounded down to a whole penny, under the same rule. Write the two functions used at the window. Each function returns both results.</p></div>
